// Q-1391 With idempotent({ transaction: false }, ...), an early `?? reply 503` (the call to a service failed) is kept like a success: the same form sent again after the service is back replays the 503 until the key expires, though the docs' own advice for a form is to send it again
// mode: run
// From FEEDBACK89.md §Q-1391 (found on 61997ab). To see it: quillo run this file with nothing on 8251
// (--service-url billing=http://127.0.0.1:8251, QUILLO_SERVICE_SECRET set), POST / with Idempotency-Key: k1 (503),
// start billing, POST again with k1: 503, idempotent-replayed: true; with Idempotency-Key: k2: 200.
// The video's apps: ~/dev/quillo-videos/videos/224-idempotent-services/app (main.qwe, billing.qwe).
service billing = "billing.qwe"
db.open("shop.db")
route POST / with http, db = idempotent({ transaction: false }, () => {
    let inv = billing.invoice("Ada", 1200) ?? reply 503 "Billing is busy"
    `Invoice #${inv.id}`
})
